# Dependency scanning scope for renv.
#
# Rationale: renv discovers dependencies by static analysis of every R file in
# the project. Third-party replication code stored as raw data, superseded
# manuscript versions, and slide decks would otherwise be recorded as if the
# paper needed them (easypackages, stargazer, WDI, plm, priceR, network,
# ggsci, revealjs, shiny). The reproducible artifact is paper_v4.Rmd plus the
# targets pipeline and scripts/; those are NOT ignored.

# Third-party replication packages kept as raw inputs
data/raw/external/

# Superseded manuscript versions
paper.Rmd
paper_v2.Rmd
paper_v3.Rmd
paper_v3_anonymous.Rmd
paper_v3_author_id.Rmd
paper_status_trade_submission.Rmd

# Slides and non-pipeline material
presentations/
Extras/
replication package/
2022-04-22/

# Working reports (gitignored; not part of the reproducible artifact).
# NOTE: scripts/diagnostics/ is deliberately NOT ignored — those scripts
# produce the CSVs the manuscript reads.
quality_reports/
coarse-output/
reports/
tmp/
